# .mill/agents — what runs on this machine.

A menu, not a rule. Nothing reads this file and it decides nothing. The
coordinator names the agent and the model for every dispatch and records the
choice in the landing commit (`.claude/skills/delegate/SKILL.md`). Copy this
file to `.mill/agents` only as a local scratch reference — `.mill/agents` is
gitignored; this example stays tracked.

## Agents

- **`omp`** — takes no `--model` flag. It reports its model, reasoning effort,
  and running cost in its own status bar; read with `orca terminal read`. Pick
  the model inside omp.

  Model selection is configured, not passed per launch. Three keys matter:

  - `modelRoles` — a record mapping role names to model ids (`plan`, `default`,
    `smol`). It is a record, so it must be set whole:
    `omp config set modelRoles '{"plan":"opencode-go/deepseek-v4-pro:high","default":"opencode-go/deepseek-v4-pro","smol":"opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash"}'`.
    The dotted form is rejected: `omp config set modelRoles.smol ...` fails.
    These ids are this machine's settings, recorded as an example of the
    mechanism, not as defaults Mill ships.
  - `prewalk.enabled` and `task.prewalk` — both `true` on this machine.
    `prewalk` switches from the active model to the `smol` role at the first
    edit/write once the plan's todo list exists, so the agent chooses the model
    from the work it observes instead of the coordinator predicting it.
- **`command-code`** — `worker-start --agent command-code` rejects `--model`.
  Its model comes from the global `~/.commandcode/config.json`, which
  command-code rewrites itself, so two dispatches on different models cannot
  run concurrently against it (#178). Set the model there first, and say so.
- **`claude`** — accepts `--model` at launch.

## Models

There is no shared registry here. Each agent exposes its own models (omp lists
its own in its status bar); the coordinator chooses per dispatch from what the
chosen agent offers.
